                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the known quantities:[[/S]][[E]]L = 80.0 cm = 0.800 m[[/E]][[E]]g = 9.8 m/s^2[[/E]][[E]]π = 3.14[[/E]][[S]](a) Period of a simple pendulum:[[/S]][[E]]T = 2π√(L/g) = 2 × 3.14 × √(0.800 / 9.8)[[/E]][[E]]T = 6.28 × √0.0816 = 6.28 × 0.2857 = 1.794 s[[/E]][[S]](b) Frequency is the reciprocal of the period:[[/S]][[E]]f = 1 / T = 1 / 1.794 = 0.557 Hz[[/E]][[A]]The period is 1.794 s and the frequency is 0.557 Hz.[[/A]]",
                    "q": "A simple oscillating pendulum has a length of 80.0 cm. Calculate its (a) Period (b) Frequency When g = 9.8 m s^-2 (1.794s, 0.557Hz)"
