                    "a": "(a) First law of reflection: the angle of incidence is equal to the angle of reflection. Second law of reflection: the incident ray, the reflected ray and the normal all lie in the same plane. (b) The mirror formula is 1/f = 1/p + 1/q, where f is the focal length of the mirror, p is the object distance and q is the image distance. (c) The negative sign in the mirror formula indicates that the distance is measured on the opposite side of the mirror from the incident light (a virtual distance): for example, a negative focal length means the mirror is convex, and a negative image distance means the image is virtual, formed behind the mirror.",
