                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the known quantities:[[/S]][[E]]q1 = q2 = e = 1.602 × 10^-19 C (charge on an electron)[[/E]][[E]]r = 1 m[[/E]][[E]]K = 9.0 × 10^9 N·m^2/C^2[[/E]][[S]]Coulomb's law:[[/S]][[E]]F = K × q1q2 / r^2[[/E]][[S]]Substitute the values:[[/S]][[E]]F = (9.0 × 10^9) × (1.602 × 10^-19) × (1.602 × 10^-19) / 1^2[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]F = 9.0 × 10^9 × 2.5664 × 10^-38 = 2.31 × 10^-28 N[[/E]][[A]]The force of repulsion between the two electrons is 2.3 × 10^-28 N. [[/A]]",
