                    "a": "[[S]]Write down the known quantities:[[/S]][[E]]ΔI/Δt = 150 A/s[[/E]][[E]]M = 5.5 × 10^-3 H[[/E]][[S]]Mutual induction:[[/S]][[E]]ε = −M × ΔI/Δt[[/E]][[S]]Substitute the values:[[/S]][[E]]ε = −(5.5 × 10^-3) × 150[[/E]][[S]]Calculate:[[/S]][[E]]ε = −0.825 V = −8.25 × 10^-1 V[[/E]][[A]]The emf induced in the surrounding coil is −0.825 V (magnitude 0.825 V). (Note: the printed answer \"(−8.25×10^-3 V)\" is wrong by a factor of 100: (5.5 × 10^-3) × 150 = 0.825, not 0.00825.)[[/A]]",
                    "q": "A coil surrounding a long solenoid, the current in the solenoid is changing at a rate of 150A/s and the mutual induction of the two coils is 5.5×10^-3H. Determine the emf induced in the surrounding coil? (−8.25×10^-3V)."
