                    "a": "In digital electronics the logic behind the working of a device is implemented by \"LOGIC GATES\". Example — a security alarm (Fig. 17.22): two switches P and Q control an alarm: [[T]]Switch \"p\"|Switch \"q\"|Alarm status;;OFF|OFF|Quiet;;ON|OFF|Quiet;;OFF|ON|Quiet;;ON|ON|Ringing[[/T]] If either switch \"P\" or \"Q\" is OFF, the alarm will remain OFF (quiet); if both switches \"P\" and \"Q\" are ON, the alarm will be ON (ringing). This table represents the logic behind the working of the alarm (an AND operation). (The book prints \"Quite\" for \"Quiet\" in this table.)",
                    "q": "(a) Explain the term \"LOGIC\" by giving a suitable example?"
