                    "a": "(No diagram can be given in this guide.) The transverse section of an angiospermic flower shows: two external wheels of leaves, the calyx (sepals) and the corolla (petals); two inner wheels, the androecium (stamens: anther and filament) and the gynoecium (carpels: stigma, style and ovary). The stamen produces pollen grains and the carpel produces the ovule in the ovary. Other parts are the receptacle, the pedicel and the pollen tube.",
