                    "a": "Over use of antibiotics can cause antibiotic resistance, in which bacteria become habitual for that antibiotic or alter their strategy to hinder the effect of the antibiotics. The change either protects the bacterium from the action of the medication or neutralizes the medication. Bacteria can acquire resistance by getting a resistance gene encoded to its chromosomes. Children given antibiotics for routine upper respiratory infections are more susceptible to aggressive antibiotic-resistant strains of the bacteria.",
