                    "a": "The Human Rights Cell is established in the Supreme Court of Pakistan. It receives direct applications from the public against the violation of human rights. The basic aim of its establishment is to give quick relief to the common people without any cost. The Cell receives applications by e-mail or post, writes letters to the concerned parties and asks for a report about the complaint, and gives quick justice to the public from the administrative side. A separate complaint cell has also been established for the applications of Pakistanis living abroad.",
                    "q": "Write a short note on the following: What is the role of Human Rights Cell established in the Supreme Court of Pakistan?"
